<UserControl x:Class="Shmoice.Tabs.HelpTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <UserControl.Resources>
        <Style x:Key="H" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,18,0,6" />
        </Style>
        <Style x:Key="P" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource BodyTextBrush}" />
            <Setter Property="LineHeight" Value="20" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,0,6" />
        </Style>
    </UserControl.Resources>
    <Grid Margin="0,12,0,0">
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="3*" />
            <ColumnDefinition Width="12" />
            <ColumnDefinition Width="2*" MinWidth="280" />
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <!-- Guide -->
        <Border Style="{StaticResource Card}" Padding="22,8,22,18">
            <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
                <StackPanel MaxWidth="760" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Getting started" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        1. In <Bold>Settings</Bold>, choose a <Bold>wake word</Bold>, a word you'd never say by accident, and your <Bold>microphone</Bold>.<LineBreak />
                        2. Check the status at the top right says <Italic>Listening</Italic>.<LineBreak />
                        3. Say the wake word, then a command: <Italic>“computer, play”</Italic>. A short pause between them is fine.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Making commands" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        In <Bold>Commands</Bold>, press ＋, type what you'll say under <Bold>When I say</Bold>, then add steps. Steps run in order;
                        <Bold>Repeat</Bold> runs one step several times (e.g. Volume up × 5 = +10%). Press <Bold>Test</Bold> to try it without speaking.
                        Changes save when you press Save or click another command.
                    </TextBlock>
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        Open the action list and type to search it, e.g. “tab” or “mute”. Hover an action to see what it does.
                        The full list is on the right.
                    </TextBlock>
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        Made a mistake? The <Bold>‹ ›</Bold> buttons at the top left undo and redo changes, and step back through the commands
                        you've opened, like a browser. (Alt+Left / Alt+Right, or your mouse's side buttons.)
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Saying something extra" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        Add a <Bold>Listen for words</Bold> step to let a command take whatever you say next. After the chime, say it;
                        later steps use it by writing <Run FontFamily="Cascadia Mono, Consolas">{heard}</Run>.
                        For example “search” = Listen for words, then Search YouTube with <Run FontFamily="Cascadia Mono, Consolas">{heard}</Run>.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Profiles: commands for specific apps" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        A profile is a list of apps, like “eldenring” or “chrome, firefox”. Commands in a profile only run while one of those
                        apps is in front, so they can't fire by accident elsewhere. The same phrase can be in several profiles and do something
                        different in each. Put a command in a profile from the <Bold>Profiles</Bold> tab, or with <Bold>Runs in</Bold> in the
                        command editor.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Schedules" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        The <Bold>Schedules</Bold> tab runs commands without speaking: at a time on chosen days (“09:00, weekdays”), or every
                        so many minutes. Shmoice has to be running. If the PC was asleep at that time, the run is skipped, not done late.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="AI Builder" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        Describe a command in plain words and Claude builds the steps. Nothing runs or saves until you test it and add it.
                        It needs your own Anthropic API key, which is stored encrypted for your Windows account.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Troubleshooting" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        <Bold>Nothing happens when I talk.</Bold> Open <Bold>Voice test</Bold>: the level bar should move when you speak. If it
                        doesn't, pick another microphone (some have a hardware mute button). If the bar moves but nothing is heard, check the wake word.
                    </TextBlock>
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        <Bold>It hears me but doesn't run.</Bold> The <Bold>History</Bold> tab says why: not sure enough (lower Min confidence in
                        Settings a little), or the command's profile app wasn't in front.
                    </TextBlock>
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        <Bold>It triggers by accident.</Bold> Raise Min confidence, use a more unusual wake word, use longer phrases, and check
                        <Bold>Voice test</Bold> for phrases that sound alike.
                    </TextBlock>
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        <Bold>Keys or clicks don't work in one app.</Bold> Windows blocks input into apps running as administrator (some games and
                        Task Manager) unless Shmoice also runs as administrator.
                    </TextBlock>

                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource H}" Text="Keyboard shortcuts" />
                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource P}">
                        Alt+Left / Alt+Right: back / forward (undo / redo)<LineBreak />
                        F2: rename the selected command · Delete: delete it<LineBreak />
                        Esc: clear a search box · Enter: leave a text box
                    </TextBlock>
                </StackPanel>
            </ScrollViewer>
        </Border>

        <!-- Every action -->
        <Border Grid.Column="2" Style="{StaticResource Card}" Padding="16">
            <DockPanel>
                <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top" Text="EVERY ACTION" Style="{StaticResource SectionLabel}" />
                <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Top" Margin="0,0,0,10">
                    <TextBox x:Name="SearchBox" TextChanged="Search_Changed" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="SearchHint" Text="Search actions…" IsHitTestVisible="False" Margin="12,0"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" FontStyle="Italic" Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}" />
                </Grid>
                <ScrollViewer VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
                    <ItemsControl x:Name="Actions">
                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                            <DataTemplate>
                                <StackPanel Margin="0,0,0,12">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Style="{StaticResource SectionLabel}" Margin="0,4,0,6" />
                                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Items}">
                                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                            <DataTemplate>
                                                <StackPanel Margin="0,0,0,8">
                                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Label}" FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Description}" TextWrapping="Wrap" FontSize="12"
                                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource MutedTextBrush}" />
                                                </StackPanel>
                                            </DataTemplate>
                                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                    </ItemsControl>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </DataTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    </ItemsControl>
                </ScrollViewer>
            </DockPanel>
        </Border>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
